(text "Hold nSLEEP low during reset. Wake with all bridges off; configure before enabling outputs.\nDisable active and passive open-load detection for logic loads. Poll fault status over SPI.\nSet each bridge OFF for input mode. High-side and low-side modes release when inactive.\nFor push-pull PWM, use complementary switching (HBx_FW); never enable both FETs continuously.\nRoute EP pad 25 to GND copper with thermal vias. Place VM/VDD decoupling close to pins.\nPWM runs inside the driver; sharing SPI with input reads does not interrupt PWM." (at 20 225 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top) ) (uuid "199df665-50d3-4b88-b998-9f16e0d45f79")) (embedded_fonts no))
